nsible; A = Accountable; C = Consulted; I = Informed | R = Responsible; A = Accountable; C = Consulted; I = Informed | R = Responsible; A = Accountable; C = Consulted; I = Informed | R = Responsible; A = Accountable; C = Consulted; I = Informed | R = Responsible; A = Accountable; C = Consulted; I = Informed | R = Responsible; A = Accountable; C = Consulted; I = Informed | R = Responsible; A = Accountable; C = Consulted; I = Informed | R = Responsible; A = Accountable; C = Consulted; I = Informed\\nActivity | BDG | CPD | IMD | TMD | IPU | URDIP | ICM | Labs / PI / Finance\\nCreate commercialisation register | A/R | C | C | R | R | C | C | R\\nCapture ECF commitment | A | C | C | C | C | C | C | R\\nValidate IP linkage | C | I | I | C | A/R | C | I | R\\nValidate TRL/CRL | C | I | C | A/R | C | C | I | R\\nMarket assessment and customer intelligence | C | I | C | C | C | A/R | C | C\\nCustomer mapping and pitch support | A/R | I | C | C | C | C | R | R\\nActual receipt confirmation | C | C | I | I | I | I | I | A/R\\nMonthly reconciliation | A/R | C | C | C | C | C | C | R\\nVariance analysis and corrective action | A/R | C | C | C | C | C | C | R\\nRoyalty monitoring | A/R | I | I | C | R | C | C | R\\nBusiness value assessment | A/R | C | C | C | C | R | C | R\\nSocial/environment impact assessment | C | C | A/R | C | I | C | C | R\\nQuarterly dashboard | A/R | R | C | C | C | C | C | R\\nAnnual impact report | A/R | R | R | C | C | C | C | R\\n\\nEvidence_Checklist\\nEvidence Checklist for ECF and Impact Claims | Evidence Checklist for ECF and Impact Claims | Evidence Checklist for ECF and Impact Claims | Evidence Checklist for ECF and Impact Claims\\nUse this to support audit-ready documentation | Use this to support audit-ready documentation | Use this to support audit-ready documentation | Use this to support audit-ready documentation\\nEvidence Type | Required For | Certified By | Remarks\\nAgreement / MoU / Licence / LoI / Work Order / Sanction | ECF commitment | Lab BD / Competent Authority\\nInvoice / Receipt / Bank Booking / Finance Certificate | Actual realisation | Lab BD\\nRoyalty Statement / Sales Statement | Royalty cases | Lab BD / IPU / Licensee\\nTechnical Milestone Certificate | Milestone-linked payments | PI / Lab\\nDeployment Certificate / User Feedback | Field deployment | PI / User / Lab\\nPilot Validation Report | Pilot/validation stage | PI / Lab / Partner\\nGovernment/PSU Adoption Letter | Mission/national deployment | IMD / Lab\\nStart-up/MSME Adoption Evidence | Socio-economic value | Lab / ICM / BDG\\nEnvironmental Measurement Report | Environmental impact | PI / Third party / Lab\\nCase Study / Media / Standards / Policy Evidence | Intangible impact | BDG / IMD / Lab\"}','{\"documentType\":\"ACTUAL_REALISATION\",\"title\":\"CSIR_ECF_Reconciliation_Value_Impact_Templates (1)\",\"summary\":\"SPREADSHEET analysed locally and mapped to SOP-03.\",\"sopStageCode\":\"SOP-03\",\"riskLevel\":\"HIGH\",\"extractedFacts\":[\"Lists\",\"Reference Lists for Dropdowns | Reference Lists for Dropdowns | Reference Lists for Dropdowns | Reference Lists for Dropdowns | Reference Lists for Dropdowns | Reference Lists for Dropdowns | Reference Lists for Dropdowns | Reference Lists for Dropdowns | Reference Lists for Dropdowns\",\"Do not delete; used for data validation | Do not delete; used for data validation | Do not delete; used for data validation | Do not delete; used for data validation | Do not delete; used for data validation | Do not delete; used for data validation | Do not delete; used for data validation | Do not delete; used for data validation | Do not delete; used for data validation\",\"Agreement_Type | Risk_Level | Status | Technology_Type | IP_Status | Commercialisation_Stage | Responsible_Unit | Escalation_Level | Impact_Category\",\"Technology Transfer | Low | Open | IP-backed | Patent granted | Lead identified | BDG | First Level | Category A - High\",\"Licensing | Medium | In Progress | Non-IP know-how | Patent filed | Under discussion | CPD | Second Level | Category B - Moderate\",\"Royalty Agreement | High | Closed | Process | Patent not filed | NDA/MoU stage | IMD | Final Review | Category C - Emerging\",\"Sponsored Research | Critical | Deferred | Product/Device | Know-how only | Agreement executed | TMD | Resolved | Category D - Monitor\"],\"financials\":[],\"technologySuggestions\":[],\"evidenceTypes\":[],\"missingFields\":[\"Lab\",\"PI / Technical Owner\",\"TRL\",\"CRL\",\"IP Status\"],\"anomalies\":[\"5 expected register field(s) were not detected.\"],\"recommendedRouteUnits\":[\"LAB_BD\",\"LAB_BD\",\"BDG\"],\"routeReason\":\"Lab BD-confirmed actual receipt and monthly reconciliation.\",\"qualityFlags\":[\"Local deterministic analysis completed.\",\"OPENAI_API_KEY is not configured; AI enrichment was skipped.\"],\"confidence\":0.68}',0.68,NULL,NULL,'2026-08-12 06:32:14.400','2026-08-12 06:32:14.818','2026-08-12 06:32:14.402'),(2,456,'COMPLETED','LOCAL_RULES',NULL,'ACTUAL_REALISATION','WORD analysed locally and mapped to SOP-03.','{\"kind\":\"WORD\",\"sections\":7,\"extractedText\":\"Council of Scientific & Industrial Research (CSIR) \\n Business Development Group (BDG), CSIR Headquarters \\n \\n STANDARD OPERATING PROCEDURE (SOP) \\n Reconciliation of Committed vs Actual Realisations, \\n External Cash Flow Commitments, and Business Value/Impact Metrics \\n across CSIR Technologies \\n \\n \\n \\n S tructured framework for systematic capturing of \\n financial, business, social, environmental, intangible and socio-economic impacts \\n arising from CSIR technologies \\n \\n \\n Document Field \\n Details \\n Document Type \\n SOP / Office Framework / Monitoring Template \\n Version \\n 1.0 - Draft for internal review \\n Date \\n 02 July 2026 \\n Nodal Unit \\n Business Development Group, CSIR HQ \\n Participating Units \\n CPD, IMD, TMD, IPU, URDIP, ICM and CSIR Laboratories \\n Applicability \\n All CSIR technologies, IP-backed and non-IP-backed, with external commercialisation or deployment value \\n \\n \\n \\n CSIR accelerated IP commercialisation blueprint and IP/non-IP commercialisation process flow, incorporating the need for early techno-economic evaluation, structured industry engagement, IP valuation, professional BD functions and governance/accountability. \\n Draft Office Note for Approval \\n \\n Subject \\n Approval sought for adoption of SOP for reconciliation of External Cash Flow commitments, actual realisations, business value and impact metrics across CSIR technologies. \\n \\n 1. Background \\n CSIR generates a significant portfolio of technologies, know-how, patents, processes, products, devices, software and service-linked offerings. However, the value generated from these outputs is often reported through separate channels such as technology transfer receipts, consultancy income, sponsored projects, royalty statements, industry collaborations, start-up adoption and mission-mode deployment. A unified and evidence-backed system is therefore required to reconcile committed external cash flow with actual realisations and to capture the wider business and societal value of CSIR technologies. \\n \\n 2. Need for the SOP \\n To reconcile committed amounts with actual receipts on a periodic and auditable basis. \\n To avoid under-reporting, duplicate reporting and fragmented reporting across units. \\n To track royalty, milestone, consultancy, sponsored research and technology transfer income in a common framework. \\n To capture indirect business value, including industry investment leveraged, import substitution, productivity gains and market creation. \\n To capture social, environmental, socio-economic and intangible impact from CSIR technologies. \\n To define clear roles for BDG, CPD, IMD, TMD, IPU, URDIP, ICM and laboratories. \\n \\n 3. Proposal \\n It is proposed to adopt the enclosed SOP and associated Excel-based templates for CSIR-wide reporting. BDG may act as the central coordinating unit for maintaining the dashboard, while CPD, IMD, TMD, IPU, URDIP and ICM may provide domain-specific validation, planning alignment, market intelligence, IP linkage, mission deployment tracking and industry outreach support. \\n 4. Approval Sought \\n Approval to circulate the SOP to all CSIR laboratories for comments and pilot implementation. \\n Approval for BDG to maintain a CSIR-wide dashboard for ECF commitments, realisations, business value and impact metrics. \\n Approval for laboratories to submit monthly reconciliation statements and quarterly impact data in the prescribed templates. \\n Approval to constitute a CSIR Commercialisation Value and Impact Monitoring Committee with representation from BDG, CPD, IMD, TMD, IPU, URDIP, ICM and laboratories. \\n \\n Submitted for kind consideration and approval. \\n \\n Table of Contents \\n \\n 1. Purpose and Scope \\n 2. Definitions \\n 3. Governance Structure \\n 4. Role Allocation \\n 5. SOP-01: Master Technology Commercialisation Register \\n 6. SOP-02: Recording of ECF Commitments \\n 7. SOP-03: Reconciliation of Committed vs Actual Realisations \\n 8. SOP-04: Business Value Capture \\n 9. SOP-05: Impact Assessment Framework \\n 10. SOP-06: Technology Impact Scoring \\n 11. SOP-07: Dashboard and Reporting \\n 12. SOP-08: Variance Management and Escalation \\n 13. SOP-09: Controls, Audit Trail and Evidence \\n 14. SOP-10: Review and Implementation \\n 15. RACI Matrix \\n 16. Annexures and Standard Templates \\n \\n 1. Purpose and Scope \\n \\n This SOP establishes a uniform CSIR-wide mechanism to record, reconcile, monitor and report External Cash Flow (ECF) commitments, actual realisations, business value and impact metrics arising from CSIR technologies. It is intended to support systematic tracking of technology transfer, licensing, royalty, consultancy, sponsored research, industry co-development, pilot deployment, government/PSU adoption, start-up/MSME adoption and social or environmental deployment. \\n \\n The SOP covers both IP-backed and non-IP-backed technologies, including patents, know-how, processes, products, software, materials, devices, instruments, biologicals, diagnostics, platforms, service-linked technologies and mission-mode deployments. \\n \\n 2. Definitions \\n Term \\n Definition \\n External Cash Flow Commitment \\n The projected or committed inflow expected from an agreement, proposal, sanction, licence, ToT, consultancy, sponsored project, milestone, royalty, pilot or co-development engagement. \\n Actual Realisation \\n The amount actually received, booked and certified by the finance function against an ECF commitment. \\n Business Value \\n The total value generated by a technology, including receipts, future royalty potential, industry investment leveraged, cost savings, import substitution, market access and strategic partnerships. \\n Impact Metrics \\n Measures of financial, social, environmental, socio-economic and intangible outcomes from technology deployment. \\n Reconciliation \\n The systematic comparison of committed/due amounts with actual receipts, along with variance explanation and corrective action. \\n At-risk ECF \\n ECF that is overdue, disputed, deferred without firm revised date, or exposed to cancellation or non-realisation risk. \\n \\n 3. Governance Structure \\n \\n A CSIR Commercialisation Value and Impact Monitoring Committee may be constituted for quarterly review. BDG shall act as the convenor and central dashboard owner. CPD, IMD, TMD, IPU, URDIP and ICM shall support planning alignment, mission deployment tracking, theme-level technology monitoring, IP linkage, techno-commercial intelligence and industry outreach respectively. \\n \\n Governance Element \\n Provision \\n Chair/Review Authority \\n As approved by competent authority at CSIR HQ. \\n Convenor \\n BDG, CSIR HQ. \\n Members \\n Representatives from CPD, IMD, TMD, IPU, URDIP, ICM and laboratories. \\n Invitees \\n Lab BD, BD Heads, IP Coordinators, PIs and sector/theme experts as required. \\n Review Frequency \\n Quarterly at CSIR HQ; monthly at laboratory level. \\n Primary Output \\n CSIR ECF Reconciliation, Business Value and Impact Dashboard. \\n \\n 4. Role Allocation \\n Unit \\n Role Allocation \\n BDG \\n Lead unit for business development, ECF reconciliation monitoring, business value capture, deal pipeline tracking, royalty follow-up dashboard and quarterly CSIR commercialisation reporting. \\n CPD \\n Align ECF and impact metrics with CSIR annual plans, institutional performance indicators, review formats and target-setting exercises. \\n IMD \\n Track innovation deployment, national mission relevance, societal deployment, public-good outcomes, start-up adoption and mission-linked impact. \\n TMD \\n Coordinate theme-wise technology pipeline, validate TRL/CRL status, monitor technology maturation and interface with Theme Directors and BD Champions. \\n IPU \\n Provide IP status, patent mapping, ownership, validity, jurisdiction, licensing history, IP bundling inputs, patent maintenance relevance and IP-linked royalty cases. \\n URDIP \\n Provide market assessment, patent landscaping, technology benchmarking, competitor mapping, commercial viability, customer intelligence and valuation inputs. \\n ICM \\n Support industry connect, sector showcases, stakeholder engagement, pitch events, follow-up with interested partners and conversion support. \\n Laboratories \\n Submit primary ECF commitment, invoice, receipt, royalty, milestone, deployment and impact data; certify data through Lab BD, PI and Finance. \\n \\n \\n 5. SOP-01: Master Technology Commercialisation Register \\n \\n Objective \\n To maintain a single source of truth for all CSIR technologies under commercialisation, deployment or external engagement. \\n \\n Key Steps / Responsibilities \\n BDG shall maintain the central register. \\n TMD and laboratories shall identify technology pipelines and validate TRL/CRL status. \\n IPU shall map IP-backed technologies, patents and know-how packages. \\n URDIP shall support techno-commercial readiness and market segmentation. \\n ICM shall support industry/customer pipeline information. \\n \\n Output \\n Technology-level master register with stage, responsible unit, commitment value, realisation status and impact category. \\n \\n 6. SOP-02: Recording of External Cash Flow Commitments \\n \\n Objective \\n To ensure that every financial commitment expected from a CSIR technology engagement is captured at the time of proposal approval, agreement execution, sanction, licence, LoI, MoU, work order or equivalent document. \\n \\n Key Steps / Responsibilities \\n Lab BD Head shall initiate entry within 7 working days. \\n PI shall certify technical scope and milestone linkage. \\n Lab BD shall validate financial terms and due dates. \\n BDG shall approve entry into the central dashboard. \\n CPD shall use the data for planning and performance review. \\n \\n Output \\n ECF Commitment Register with due-date-wise payment schedule and responsibility mapping. \\n \\n 7. SOP-03: Reconciliation of Committed vs Actual Realisations \\n \\n Objective \\n To compare committed and due amounts with actual receipts and record variances, reasons, corrective actions and revised timelines. \\n \\n Key Steps / Responsibilities \\n Lab BD shall provide monthly actual receipts. \\n Lab BD shall map receipts to commitment entries. \\n PI shall certify milestone achievement wherever payments are milestone-linked. \\n BDG shall consolidate and analyse laboratory-wise, theme-wise and CSIR-level reconciliation. \\n CPD, TMD, IPU, URDIP, ICM and IMD shall provide corrective support as per issue type. \\n \\n Output \\n Monthly lab reconciliation and quarterly CSIR-level ECF reconciliation statemen \\n \\n 8. SOP-04: Business Value Capture \\n \\n Objective \\n To capture the full business value of CSIR technologies beyond immediate receipts. \\n \\n Key Steps / Responsibilities \\n BDG shall consolidate business value metrics. \\n URDIP shall support market value, competitive positioning and benchmarking. \\n IPU shall support IP value and licensing potential. \\n TMD shall validate technical maturity and scale-up potential. \\n ICM shall capture partner feedback and market interest. \\n \\n Output \\n Business value dashboard including direct revenue, indirect financial value, market value, strategic value and long-term revenue potential. \\n 9. SOP-05: Impact Assessment Framework \\n \\n Objective \\n To capture financial, social, environmental, socio-economic, strategic and intangible impact from technology deployment. \\n \\n Key Steps / Responsibilities \\n IMD shall lead mission, social and public-good impact classification. \\n BDG shall integrate impact metrics into the commercialisation dashboard. \\n PIs and labs shall provide evidence-backed impact statements. \\n URDIP shall support socio-economic and market context. \\n CPD shall align impact reporting with institutional reporting. \\n \\n Output \\n Technology impact profile with evidence, beneficiary data, environmental benefits and intangible outcomes. \\n \\n 10. SOP-06: Technology Impact Scoring \\n \\n Objective \\n To score technologies annually using a consistent 100-point framework for business value and impact. \\n \\n Key Steps / Responsibilities \\n BDG shall coordinate scoring. \\n TMD shall validate maturity and scalability. \\n IMD shall validate social/mission impact. \\n URDIP shall validate market and indirect value. \\n IPU shall validate IP/licensing dimensions. \\n \\n Output \\n Category A, B, C and D classification for prioritisation, scaling, repositioning or monitoring. \\n \\n 11. SOP-07: Dashboard and Reporting \\n \\n Objective \\n To produce technology-level, lab-level, theme-level and CSIR-level dashboards. \\n Key Steps / Responsibilities \\n BDG shall maintain and circulate quarterly dashboards. \\n CPD shall integrate data with performance review formats. \\n Labs shall submit monthly and quarterly data as per templates. \\n Dashboard indicators shall include ECF committed, actual realised, overdue amount, at-risk amount, technologies licensed, technologies deployed, royalty cases and impact outcomes. \\n \\n Output \\n Quarterly CSIR Commercialisation Value and Impact Dashboard. \\n \\n 12. SOP-08: Variance Management and Escalation \\n \\n Objective \\n To define action pathways for overdue, disputed, deferred, under-verified or cancelled commitments. \\n \\n Key Steps / Responsibilities \\n Lab BD and Finance shall identify variance reasons. \\n BDG shall classify at-risk ECF and monitor corrective actions. \\n ICM shall support industry follow-up. \\n IPU shall support royalty and licensing-related issues. \\n TMD shall support technology milestone issues. \\n URDIP shall support valuation or market repositioning issues. \\n \\n Output \\n Variance closure tracker with owner, revised date and escalation status. \\n \\n 13. SOP-09: Controls, Audit Trail and Evidence \\n \\n Objective \\n To ensure that commitments, realisations and impact claims are evidence-backed and auditable. \\n \\n Key Steps / Responsibilities \\n No commitment shall be counted without agreement, sanction, work order, licence, LoI, MoU or equivalent evidence. \\n No realisation shall be counted without Lab BD certification. \\n No impact claim shall be reported without evidence certified by PI or authorised lab representative. \\n BDG shall maintain version-controlled dashboards and digital archives. \\n \\n Output \\n Audit-ready file containing commitment evidence, receipt evidence, milestone evidence and impact evidence. \\n \\n 14. SOP-10: Review and Implementation \\n \\n Objective \\n To implement the SOP in a phased and manageable manner across CSIR. \\n \\n Key Steps / Responsibilities \\n Month 1: circulate SOP and templates to labs. \\n Months 2-3: pilot in selected high-commercialisation labs/themes. \\n Month 4: refine formats and issue final reporting instructions. \\n Quarter 2 onwards: implement quarterly CSIR dashboard. \\n Annual: publish consolidated business value and impact report. \\n \\n Output \\n Phased implementation plan with pilot learnings and final dashboard roll-out. \\n \\n \\n 15. RACI Matrix \\n \\n R = Responsible; A = Accountable; C = Consulted; I = Informed. \\n \\n Activity \\n BDG \\n CPD \\n IMD \\n TMD \\n IPU \\n URDIP \\n ICM \\n Labs/PI/ \\n Finance \\n Create commercialisation register \\n A/R \\n C \\n C \\n R \\n R \\n C \\n C \\n R \\n Capture ECF commitment \\n A \\n C \\n C \\n C \\n C \\n C \\n C \\n R \\n Validate IP linkage \\n C \\n I \\n I \\n C \\n A/R \\n C \\n I \\n R \\n Validate TRL/CRL \\n C \\n I \\n C \\n A/R \\n C \\n C \\n I \\n R \\n Market assessment and customer intelligence \\n C \\n I \\n C \\n C \\n C \\n A/R \\n C \\n C \\n Customer mapping and pitch support \\n A/R \\n I \\n C \\n C \\n C \\n C \\n R \\n R \\n Actual receipt confirmation \\n C \\n C \\n I \\n I \\n I \\n I \\n I \\n A/R \\n Monthly reconciliation \\n A/R \\n C \\n C \\n C \\n C \\n C \\n C \\n R \\n Variance analysis and corrective action \\n A/R \\n C \\n C \\n C \\n C \\n C \\n C \\n R \\n Royalty monitoring \\n A/R \\n I \\n I \\n C \\n R \\n C \\n C \\n R \\n Business value assessment \\n A/R \\n C \\n C \\n C \\n C \\n R \\n C \\n R \\n Social/environment impact assessment \\n C \\n C \\n A/R \\n C \\n I \\n C \\n C \\n R \\n Quarterly dashboard \\n A/R \\n R \\n C \\n C \\n C \\n C \\n C \\n R \\n Annual impact report \\n A/R \\n R \\n R \\n C \\n C \\n C \\n C \\n R \\n \\n \\n 16. Annexures and Standard Templates \\n \\n The following standard templates shall be maintained in Excel format. The templates may be used by laboratories for monthly submission and by BDG for consolidation. \\n \\n Annexure \\n Template \\n Purpose \\n Annexure I \\n Master Technology Commercialisation Register \\n Technology identity, lab, PI, TRL/CRL, IP status, sector, stage and responsible officers. \\n Annexure II \\n External Cash Flow Commitment Register \\n Committed amount, payment schedule, milestones, agreement reference and due dates. \\n Annexure III \\n Actual Realisation Register \\n Amount due, amount received, receipt reference, balance, delay days and finance certification. \\n Annexure IV \\n Variance Analysis Register \\n Variance reason, corrective action, owner, revised date and escalation status. \\n Annexure V \\n Business Value Capture Format \\n Direct revenue, future royalty potential, industry investment, import substitution and market value. \\n Annexure VI \\n Impact Metrics Format \\n Social, environmental, socio-economic, strategic and intangible impact indicators. \\n Annexure VII \\n Risk and Escalation Tracker \\n At-risk ECF, bottlenecks, escalation level and closure status. \\n Annexure VIII \\n Dashboard Summary \\n Lab-wise, theme-wise and CSIR-level summary indicators. \\n \\n Mandatory Data Dictionary \\n Field \\n Description \\n Technology Name \\n Official title of technology/know-how/product/process. \\n Technology Type \\n IP-backed, non-IP, process, device, material, software, service-linked or platform. \\n Sector/Theme \\n Relevant CSIR sector and theme. \\n TRL/CRL \\n Validated technology and commercial readiness status. \\n Partner \\n Industry, PSU, government, start-up, MSME or social-sector adopter. \\n Agreement Type \\n Licence, ToT, consultancy, sponsored research, pilot, validation, co- development or other. \\n Committed Amount \\n Total financial commitment expected from the engagement. \\n Amount Due \\n Amount due as per payment schedule up to reporting date. \\n Actual Receipt \\n Amount actually received and certified by Finance. \\n Variance Reason \\n Reason for non-realisation, delay, partial receipt or excess receipt. \\n Impact Evidence \\n Evidence supporting financial, social, environmental or other impact claims. \\n \\n Scoring Matrix \\n Parameter \\n Weightage \\n Direct financial realisation \\n 20 \\n Future revenue/royalty potential \\n 10 \\n Industry adoption and market traction \\n 15 \\n Strategic/national relevance \\n 10 \\n Social impact \\n 10 \\n Environmental impact \\n 10 \\n Import substitution/export potential \\n 10 \\n Scalability and replication potential \\n 10 \\n Intangible institutional value \\n 5 \\n Total \\n 100 \\n Technology scoring categories: Category A above 75; Category B 50-75; Category C 30-50; Category D below 30. \\n \\n Evidence Checklist \\n \\n Agreement, MoU, licence , LoI , sanction order, work order or approved proposal. \\n Invoice, receipt reference, bank/finance booking or finance certification. \\n Royalty statement, licensee sales statement or milestone completion certificate. \\n PI certificate for technical milestone achievement or deployment status. \\n Industry deployment certificate, user feedback, field validation or pilot report. \\n Government/PSU adoption letter, start-up/MSME adoption evidence or case study. \\n Environmental savings, social beneficiary, livelihood, health or socio-economic impact evidence. \\n Media, standards, policy influence or recognition evidence for intangible value. \\n \\n Indicative Implementation Timeline \\n Timeline \\n Action \\n Month 1 \\n Issue SOP and Excel templates; nominate lab nodal officers; create baseline register. \\n Months 2-3 \\n Pilot the format with selected technologies/labs/themes; validate finance and impact data. \\n Month 4 \\n Refine data fields, issue final instructions, begin quarterly CSIR dashboard. \\n Quarter 2 onwards \\n Full quarterly reconciliation and impact reporting across labs. \\n Annual \\n Prepare CSIR Commercialisation Business Value and Impact Report. \\n \\n Closing Note \\n \\n This SOP enables CSIR to move from fragmented activity reporting to integrated value and impact reporting. It will support stronger accountability, better realisation of committed external cash flow, evidence-based commercialisation monitoring and a more comprehensive demonstration of the financial, societal, environmental and strategic value generated by CSIR technologies.\\n\\nCSIR - SOP for ECF Reconciliation, Business Value and Impact Metrics\\n\\nInternal draft for review and approval | Version 1.0\\n\\nCSIR - SOP for ECF Reconciliation, Business Value and Impact Metrics\\n\\nCSIR - SOP for ECF Reconciliation, Business Value and Impact Metrics\\n\\nInternal draft for review and approval | Version 1.0\\n\\nInternal draft for review and approval | Version 1.0\"}','{\"documentType\":\"ACTUAL_REALISATION\",\"title\":\"CSIR_SOP_ECF_Reconciliation_Value_Impact_Framework (1)\",\"summary\":\"WORD analysed locally and mapped to SOP-03.\",\"sopStageCode\":\"SOP-03\",\"riskLevel\":\"HIGH\",\"extractedFacts\":[\"Council of Scientific & Industrial Research (CSIR) \",\" Business Development Group (BDG), CSIR Headquarters \",\" \",\" STANDARD OPERATING PROCEDURE (SOP) \",\" Reconciliation of Committed vs Actual Realisations, \",\" External Cash Flow Commitments, and Business Value/Impact Metrics \",\" across CSIR Technologies \",\" \"],\"financials\":[],\"technologySuggestions\":[],\"evidenceTypes\":[],\"missingFields\":[],\"anomalies\":[],\"recommendedRouteUnits\":[\"LAB_BD\",\"LAB_BD\",\"BDG\"],\"routeReason\":\"Lab BD-confirmed actual receipt and monthly reconciliation.\",\"qualityFlags\":[\"Local deterministic analysis completed.\",\"OPENAI_API_KEY is not configured; AI enrichment was skipped.\"],\"confidence\":0.68}',0.68,NULL,3,'2026-08-12 06:33:26.085','2026-08-12 06:33:26.147','2026-08-12 06:33:26.087');
