0 | 0\\n6 | Used Cooking Oil from Hotels and Restaurants | 1 | 1 | 0\\n7 | Utilization of Treated Water from Sewage Treatment Plants | 0 | 0 | 0\\n\\nTechnology Master\\nTechnology Master Sheet |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | \\nTopic | Fit | Lab | Technology Title | Solution and Raw Material | Conversion / Recovery / Performance | IP Status | TRL | Techno-economics | Scale-up Potential | Industry Engagement | Mapping Note\\nConstruction and Demolition (C&D) Waste Solutions | Related | CSIR-AMPRI | Marble Composite Technology | Converts marble waste with agro/industrial waste into glossy hybrid composite boards and wood-substitute products for building and interior applications. | Positioned as cheaper than teak wood, with glossy finish and variable-density composite products for construction and furnishing use. | Multiple granted patents/filings across India, USA, South Africa, Malaysia and other jurisdictions; includes 201811016873 and 201811047389. | TRL 7; CRL 3-4. | Techno-economic note states the product is cheaper than teak wood. | Licensed to Eco Bright Sheet Pvt. Ltd., Amit Densified Door Pvt. Ltd., and Shubh Green Pvt. Ltd.; client plant-capacity details under process. | Already licensed, non-exclusive; commercialized with multiple industry partners. | Mapped as related to the C&D/construction stream because it valorizes marble waste into construction-oriented composite products.\\nSteel Slag Utilization | Direct | CSIR-CECRI | Extraction of Metal Values from Ferro-Chrome with Zero-Chrome Discharge | Integrated pyro-hydrometallurgical valorization of ferrochrome slag for selective recovery of magnesium, chromium, aluminium, and silica-rich residue. | Achieves about 95% magnesium extraction, produces >95% MgCl2 and an essentially chromium-free residue suitable for construction materials; optional conversion to ~98% pure metallic magnesium. | Patent filed; ownership with CSIR; FTO not conducted. | TRL 6 with 25 kg/batch pilot validation. | Uses commercially available chemicals and conventional operations; market potential marked above Rs. 100 Cr. | Pilot-scale demonstration completed at 25 kg ferrochrome slag per batch with industrially sourced material. | Industry interest from TATA Steels and SAIL; ready for licensing on a non-exclusive basis. | Strong direct fit for steel-slag utilization because it recovers critical metals before enabling safe reuse of the final residue.\\nSteel Slag Utilization | Related | Not specified in source | Recovery of Remnant Iron from Induction Furnace Slag | Jaw crushing and magnetic separation of induction-furnace slag to recover entrapped iron for recycle back to the furnace. | Improves metal recovery and reduces raw-material consumption by recovering remnant iron from cooled furnace slag. | Not stated in source. | Industrial process description; explicit TRL not stated. | Value comes from recycling remnant iron back into the metallic charge and lowering slag-disposal burden. | Described as part of a continuous steelmaking route using induction furnace, CCM, and rolling mill operations. | Industry deployment details not separately stated. | Mapped as a related steel-slag-utilization route because it focuses on slag beneficiation and iron recovery rather than a standalone licensable technology brief.\\nBrine Sludge from Chlor-Alkali Industries | Direct | Not specified in source | Advanced Flexible and Moldable Composite Material - Brine Sludge-Derived | Converts chlor-alkali brine sludge with additives into flexible composite sheets and shielding/sealant products for stru\",\"engine\":\"PYTHON_MATCHER_V1\",\"needKeywords\":[\"waste\",\"direct\",\"plastic\",\"not\",\"trl\",\"oil\",\"pet\",\"into\",\"slag\",\"used\",\"cooking\",\"composite\",\"fit\",\"about\",\"packaging\",\"patent\",\"flexible\",\"recovery\",\"related\",\"products\",\"deployment\",\"because\",\"stated\",\"saf\",\"topic\",\"source\",\"licensed\",\"application\",\"yet\",\"techno-economic\"],\"matches\":[{\"source\":\"UPLOADED_FILE\",\"technologyId\":null,\"name\":\"Extraction of Metal Values from Ferro-Chrome with Zero-Chrome Discharge\",\"labCode\":\"CECRI\",\"labName\":\"CSIR-CECRI\",\"score\":95,\"matchedTerms\":[\"Steel Slag Utilization\"],\"readiness\":\"Ready to sell / transfer\",\"trl\":6,\"commercialisationStage\":\"Industry interest from TATA Steels and SAIL; ready for licensing on a non-exclusive basis.\",\"reason\":\"Direct match from uploaded Technology Master sheet · Integrated pyro-hydrometallurgical valorization of ferrochrome slag for selective recovery of magnesium, chromium, aluminium, and silica-rich residue.\"},{\"source\":\"UPLOADED_FILE\",\"technologyId\":null,\"name\":\"Advanced Flexible and Moldable Composite Material - Brine Sludge-Derived\",\"labCode\":\"Not specified in source\",\"labName\":\"Not specified in source\",\"score\":95,\"matchedTerms\":[\"Brine Sludge from Chlor-Alkali Industries\"],\"readiness\":\"Ready to sell / transfer\",\"trl\":4,\"commercialisationStage\":\"Not yet commercialized or deployed; non-exclusive licensing preference stated.\",\"reason\":\"Direct match from uploaded Technology Master sheet · Converts chlor-alkali brine sludge with additives into flexible composite sheets and shielding/sealant products for structural and industrial use.\"},{\"source\":\"UPLOADED_FILE\",\"technologyId\":null,\"name\":\"AI-enabled NIR-based Automated Rigid Plastic Waste Identification and Sorting System\",\"labCode\":\"CEERI Chennai Centre\",\"labName\":\"CSIR-CEERI Chennai Centre\",\"score\":95,\"matchedTerms\":[\"Plastic Waste (Multi-Layered Packaging, PET, Shrink PET, PVC Wrappers)\"],\"readiness\":\"Ready to sell / transfer\",\"trl\":5,\"commercialisationStage\":\"Not licensed or commercialized yet.\",\"reason\":\"Direct match from uploaded Technology Master sheet · AI-enabled near-infrared spectroscopy system for rapid, non-contact identification and automated sorting of rigid post-consumer plastic waste.\"},{\"source\":\"UPLOADED_FILE\",\"tec