h 100% recycled aggregate achieve 18 MPa compressive strength at about Rs. 8 overall cost per brick; hollow blocks achieve 4.5 MPa with overall cost about Rs. 26 per block. | No IPR stated; commercialization/licensed ownership note marked NIL; jurisdiction India. | TRL not explicitly selected in the source form; validation and pilot fields were left unmarked. | Production cost is comparable to commercial fly-ash and burnt-clay bricks; well suited to small-scale industries. | Can be produced using existing commercial fly-ash brick and hollow-block manufacturing facilities, with size variation possible for blocks. | Target customers include government housing agencies, PWDs, contractors, and infrastructure developers; industry-interest fields were left unmarked. | Direct C&D-waste solution because it uses recycled aggregate from demolition waste with industrial by-products to produce construction bricks and blocks.\\nConstruction and Demolition (C&D) Waste Solutions | Related | CSIR-AMPRI | Marble Composite Technology | Converts marble waste with agro/industrial waste into glossy hybrid composite boards and wood-substitute products for building and interior applications. | Positioned as cheaper than teak wood, with glossy finish and variable-density composite products for construction and furnishing use. | Multiple granted patents/filings across India, USA, South Africa, Malaysia and other jurisdictions; includes 201811016873 and 201811047389. | TRL 7; CRL 3-4. | Techno-economic note states the product is cheaper than teak wood. | Licensed to Eco Bright Sheet Pvt. Ltd., Amit Densified Door Pvt. Ltd., and Shubh Green Pvt. Ltd.; client plant-capacity details under process. | Already licensed, non-exclusive; commercialized with multiple industry partners. | Mapped as related to the C&D/construction stream because it valorizes marble waste into construction-oriented composite products.\\nSteel Slag Utilization | Direct | CSIR-CECRI | Extraction of Metal Values from Ferro-Chrome with Zero-Chrome Discharge | Integrated pyro-hydrometallurgical valorization of ferrochrome slag for selective recovery of magnesium, chromium, aluminium, and silica-rich residue. | Achieves about 95% magnesium extraction, produces >95% MgCl2 and an essentially chromium-free residue suitable for construction materials; optional conversion to ~98% pure metallic magnesium. | Patent filed; ownership with CSIR; FTO not conducted. | TRL 6 with 25 kg/batch pilot validation. | Uses commercially available chemicals and conventional operations; market potential marked above Rs. 100 Cr. | Pilot-scale demonstration completed at 25 kg ferrochrome slag per batch with industrially sourced material. | Industry interest from TATA Steels and SAIL; ready for licensing on a non-exclusive basis. | Strong direct fit for st\",\"engine\":\"PYTHON_MATCHER_V1\",\"needKeywords\":[\"waste\",\"direct\",\"not\",\"plastic\",\"trl\",\"slag\",\"about\",\"pet\",\"into\",\"oil\",\"used\",\"composite\",\"construction\",\"cooking\",\"flexible\",\"stated\",\"patent\",\"fit\",\"packaging\",\"recovery\",\"related\",\"because\",\"products\",\"topic\",\"deployment\",\"industrial\",\"saf\",\"source\",\"recycled\",\"furnace\"],\"matches\":[{\"source\":\"UPLOADED_FILE\",\"technologyId\":null,\"name\":\"Eco-friendly Recycled Aggregate Bricks and Hollow Blocks\",\"labCode\":\"SERC\",\"labName\":\"CSIR-SERC\",\"score\":95,\"matchedTerms\":[\"Construction and Demolition (C&D) Waste Solutions\"],\"readiness\":\"Needs technical/commercial review\",\"trl\":null,\"commercialisationStage\":\"Target customers include government housing agencies, PWDs, contractors, and infrastructure developers; industry-interest fields were left unmarked.\",\"reason\":\"Direct match from uploaded Technology Master sheet · Slag-cement-based recycled aggregate bricks and hollow blocks made using recycled aggregate, recycled sand, fly ash, and slag cement for masonry and infill construction applications.\"},{\"source\":\"UPLOADED_F